# Copy to `.dev.vars` for local `wrangler pages dev`. That file is gitignored.
#
# In production these are Pages secrets, set with:
#   npx wrangler pages secret put <NAME> --project-name akademia-dermatoskopii
#
# Nothing here is a real credential — do not put one in this file.

# --- Registration form (/zapisy/) -------------------------------------------

# Turnstile secret, paired with TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY in src/consts.ts.
# The value below is Cloudflare's documented "always passes" TEST secret.
# /api/register fails closed if this is unset, so the form stops working rather
# than accepting unverified submissions.
TURNSTILE_SECRET=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA

# --- Registration admin (/admin-rejestracje/) -------------------------------
#
# Cloudflare Access application details. Both are required; the admin
# middleware refuses every request unless it can verify a signed Access JWT.
# Left unset here on purpose: locally the admin panel returns 403, which is the
# correct behaviour rather than a bypass.
#
# ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=<your-team>.cloudflareaccess.com
# ACCESS_AUD=<Application Audience (AUD) Tag from the Access app>

# Recommended second gate: comma-separated allowlist checked after the Access
# JWT verifies. Guards against a mistyped Access policy widening access to
# registrant data. Unset = trust the Access policy alone (logs a warning).
# ADMIN_EMAILS=jacek@example.com,olga@example.com

# --- Sveltia CMS (/admin/) --------------------------------------------------
#
# GitHub OAuth app used by the CMS. Only needed if you are working on the CMS
# login flow locally.
#
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GITHUB_OAUTH_SCOPE=repo

# --- Not an environment variable --------------------------------------------
#
# Email sending uses the MAILER service binding (workers/mailer), not a token.
# Under `wrangler pages dev` that binding is absent, so registration emails
# fail and are logged — the D1 row is still written, by design.
